==Battleground==
*10 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*2 [[Mistress Celeboodle]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*5 [[Helmut Krabbe]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Casaurian Darkjo]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Casaurian Ahirujo]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*4 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Having all of the [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] from [[Into the Future]] is essentially required for this stage, otherwise the Aliens become nearly impossible to deal with.

This stage is significantly easier than the previous stage, [[Venomous Duck]], due to you getting significantly more money overall.

Since the main enemies are the Casaurian Darkjo and Casaurian Ahirujo, all you will really need is [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and of course something good against Red and Black. [[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]] could be good here if you're able to hold the line (for example by using [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]). [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] is optional due to the fact it isn't as good at stalling with Casaurian Darkjo in the level.

